rewrite:
My throat is dust, my mouth is dry;
A frosty cup calls, and I comply.
A gulp of frost runs through my jaw;
My aching gums cry out for thaw.
I gasp and laugh, my thirst still strong;
How can such joy hurt all day long?
A sip too far, a chill too bold:
I want its frost and shun its cold.

